1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,537
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,677
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,837
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,797
I'm really, really stuck on you, oh, oh.

13
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,980
Believe in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,577
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,937
Live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:33,537
There is no limit to us,
we have the power of love.

22
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,677
So we don't wanna live ordinary lives.

23
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:39,797
We have a chance to live in paradise.

24
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,700
We believe in one another.

25
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:56,600
We've got trouble!

26
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,980
Vivi, where are they?

27
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,100
Oh, Igaram, what is it?

28
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,817
Luffy and all the others.

29
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:12,782
Where are they?

30
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,430
The sea.

31
00:02:14,513 --> 00:02:15,343
They are pirates.

32
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:17,500
Oh, no.

33
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:20,700
Listen up, you guys.

34
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,277
Pirates are nothing but scum.

35
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,419
Every one of them.

36
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:24,700
Hey, wait.

37
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:25,717
Don't you remember?

38
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,717
What are you saying? Come on.

39
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,000
You used to be one. You're right!

40
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,060
How could I forget? Ah-ha!

41
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,240
Oh, baby! Let's dance!

42
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,220
Ah, yeah! Dance! Dance!

43
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:38,690
That's right!

44
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:39,997
In the fucking style!

45
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,609
We're all on our way back!

46
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,957
It looks like those two
subdued the enemy ship.

47
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,457
It took them long enough.

48
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:47,370
Don't tell me.

49
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:48,717
They're dancing, right?

50
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,997
I trusted those two to finish off that
pirate ship that tried to escape us,

51
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,537
and this is what they do.

52
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:54,450
Disappointed.

53
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:55,716
Hina's disappointed.

54
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:57,757
Have you finished deploying all the ships?

55
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,137
Yes, that's affirmative, ma 'am.

56
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:02,926
Every harbor in this dust bowl
of the country is now blockaded.

57
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:07,580
But, ma 'am, there's one thing
I'm concerned about. What's that?

58
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:10,057
Well, it's just the
Straw Hatch ship, ma 'am.

59
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:13,375
It was confirmed to be near
Aramalu, and now it's gone.

60
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,577
Don't tell me they've
left the country already.

61
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:17,131
No, I doubt that, ma 'am.

62
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:18,514
Then go search for it.

63
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,877
Scour the entire coast.

64
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,901
Yes, right away.

65
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:22,210
Oh, no.

66
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,897
Miss Hina, we're sorry it took us so long.

67
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:27,197
Aren't you gonna ask
us why it took so long?

68
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,574
Why'd it take so long?

69
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:31,417
Because we were picking these
flowers for you, Miss Hina.

70
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,330
No, thanks.

71
00:03:32,413 --> 00:03:33,637
Now, man your positions right away.

72
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,997
We're going after the Straw Hat Pirates.

73
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,260
The Straw Hats?

74
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:42,610
Not bad.

75
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,546
So, a final farewell,
old kingdom of the sand.

76
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,877
Lupi, aren't you full yet?

77
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:49,517
These Alabasta dishes are
great, aren't they, Sanji?

78
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:50,677
You should make them sometime.

79
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:54,037
Yeah, I like them too, so I got
some recipes from terracotta.

80
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:56,297
I also got some of their local spices.

81
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:58,680
Um, what's wrong, Nami? Are you sick?

82
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:03,917
I'll give you a piece of this if
you want, but just a small one.

83
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,294
Nami, if you're thinking about
Vivi again, I understand.

84
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:10,811
Listen, moping around about it won't help.

85
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,117
I know it must be really hard for you.

86
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,259
You two got close.

87
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,440
Just keep your chin up, okay?

88
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:18,660
That's not bad.

89
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:25,780
I'm just sad we didn't take the reward.

90
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:27,740
The one billion berries.

91
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,800
You're moping about the money?!

92
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,437
Usopp fell off!

93
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,897
You shouldn't mislead
people like that, Nami!

94
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,397
What did you think I was upset about?

95
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:39,777
We just walked away from a huge
payday that we actually earned!

96
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,180
Usopp fell down!

97
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:42,458
That's his problem!

98
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,120
But you caused it!

99
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,620
Conney, wake up! You're needed!

100
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:50,817
It's no use, Igaram.

101
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:53,497
But the world government has
released new bounties on their heads!

102
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:54,977
We should at least warn them.

103
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:56,857
I had the duck squadron take them.

104
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:59,857
Even if Karoo could catch up to
them, it wouldn't change anything.

105
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:00,920
Why's that?

106
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,797
Those new bounties, they'll
actually make them happy?

107
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,217
They'll all be tickled pink!

108
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:06,317
But princess, they...

109
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,537
Trust me, they'll be fine.

110
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,497
Now out you go!

111
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,037
I've got to get some rest.

112
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,297
I've got a big day tomorrow, remember?

113
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:16,620
Oh that's right Your coming of age
ceremony is tomorrow morning at ten.

114
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,217
Uh-huh.

115
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:19,437
Now, come on, Karoo.

116
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:20,755
Let's get some sleep.

117
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,920
Something's bothering me. Hey!

118
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,200
She's awfully calm.

119
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:36,330
Strange.

120
00:05:36,413 --> 00:05:37,360
Very strange.

121
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,080
It's really quiet, isn't it, Karoo?

122
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:50,422
We haven't had a night
this quiet in a long time.

123
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:56,238
The cook who guards the refrigerator
from a late-night raider is gone.

124
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:59,245
So too is the swordsman
who trains every night.

125
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:02,400
The navigator who throws
pillows when she's asleep.

126
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,240
Or two, they're gone.

127
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:12,540
Snail communication? From who? Don't know.

128
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,757
He called himself Bon.

129
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:15,160
Just Bon? That's it?

130
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,677
Uh, never heard of the guy.

131
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:17,590
That's strange.

132
00:06:17,673 --> 00:06:19,697
He insists that you're all good friends.

133
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:20,820
Friends with us?

134
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:23,610
Hello?

135
00:06:23,693 --> 00:06:25,160
Hey, old friends, it's me!

136
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:29,988
I bet you never thought you'd
hear from me again, didn't you?

137
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,760
You freak! Shut up!

138
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,480
So you escaped Mr.

139
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:36,637
Two, and what do you want?

140
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,550
Straw Hat!

141
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,640
I'd recognize that force anywhere!

142
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:41,272
You're right, I escaped.

143
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,237
And I want to keep it that
way, so don't call me Mr.

144
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,150
Two.

145
00:06:45,233 --> 00:06:46,377
If the Marines intercept this call,

146
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:49,797
they'll be able to ascertain the
locations of both me and you.

147
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:51,233
Thanks a lot, you jerk!

148
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,614
Tell us what you want.

149
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:54,311
Oh, it's not what I want.

150
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:57,340
It's what I have! Your ship! Stop joking!

151
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,377
I'm gonna kick your butt for saying that!

152
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:00,290
Where are you?

153
00:07:00,373 --> 00:07:01,945
On your ship, the Going Merry!

154
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:03,777
I should have kicked him harder.

155
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:05,440
Hey! Call down!

156
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:06,850
Please!

157
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:11,200
I mean, we are friends, right? Right!

158
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,888
He's at the upper part
of the Sandora River.

159
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,480
Can we trust him?

160
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:24,277
We did become friends
that one time, but...

161
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:26,637
That was before we knew he
was part of Baroque Works.

162
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,097
I guess we have no choice. You're right.

163
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:30,220
He has our ship.

164
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:33,997
If he tries to trick us, I'll be more than
happy to kick the crap out of him again.

165
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,551
All right, we gotta move.

166
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:37,080
Hey, you guys.

167
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:43,420
I, uh, I don't...

168
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:46,240
I don't know what to do.

169
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:49,240
If you were me, what would you do?

170
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:54,364
VV, we can give you 12
hours to make a decision.

171
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:56,705
We'll travel down the Sandora,

172
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,817
after teaching Ballerina Boy
why he shouldn't steal from us,

173
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,497
and by noon tomorrow, we'll
draw near the Eastern Harbor.

174
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,757
I doubt we'll be able
to drop anchor, though.

175
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,500
If you do decide to join us,

176
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:09,097
that's going to be the only
chance for you to come aboard.

177
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,497
Twelve o 'clock on the dot.

178
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:11,580
It's your choice.

179
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,480
You could stay a princess
or become a pirate.

180
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:17,857
I'm sure being a pirate doesn't
compare to being a princess,

181
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:19,277
but we'd sure love to have you.

182
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,397
Yeah, so why wait?

183
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,637
Come with us now, Vivi!

184
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,896
Knock it off, Luffy.

185
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,160
Yeah, come on. Why?

186
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:25,917
Don't you guys want her to join us?

187
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,412
We do, but that's something
she has to decide for herself.

188
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:35,848
Twelve o 'clock on the dot.

189
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:40,237
If it's the eastern harbor, it'll
take four hours to get there on Karoo.

190
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:42,967
If I left here by eight,
I'd make it on time.

191
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,580
Life is a pirate, huh?

192
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:48,853
Adventures on the high seas,
surrounded by loyal friends?

193
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:50,097
If I miss this chance,

194
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:54,062
I know I'll never get another one
like it for the rest of my life.

195
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:57,719
On the other hand, I have
duties here as a princess,

196
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:02,101
and at a critical time since this
land's in the midst of a rebirth.

197
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:09,020
Whatever I do choose, you'll
stay with me, won't you?

198
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:16,920
Say, Karoo, what would you like to do?

199
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:20,910
Finally!

200
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,806
Long time no see, my friends!

201
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,902
Did you guys miss little old me?

202
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:25,980
Not a bit.

203
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:28,100
Let's unload. Later, ducks.

204
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,217
Thanks for the lift.

205
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:31,437
Yeah, you ducks take care of yourselves!

206
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,677
Have a safe trip.

207
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:36,337
Say bye to the king, the old tube-haired
guy, and all the others for us!

208
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:37,361
Come on, fellas!

209
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:39,350
Farewell!

210
00:09:39,433 --> 00:09:43,100
May you ugly ducklings
turn into beautiful swans!

211
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,860
Wait! Hold on! Yeah, what?

212
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,017
Don't dare want me!

213
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:49,930
That's just rude!

214
00:09:50,013 --> 00:09:51,317
You should learn some manners, pretty boy!

215
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,577
Friends aren't supposed to
talk to their friends that way!

216
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:55,057
Quit saying that, you weirdo!

217
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,377
We're not friends, we're enemies!

218
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:57,290
You lied to us!

219
00:09:57,373 --> 00:09:58,203
No, I didn't!

220
00:09:58,286 --> 00:10:00,557
I just didn't mention that I
was a member of Baroque Works!

221
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:03,581
Besides, none of that
really matters now, does it?

222
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:05,545
Baroque works is done for now.

223
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:08,217
And that means that
we're no longer enemies.

224
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,130
Hey, move it.

225
00:10:09,213 --> 00:10:10,043
Oh, my bad.

226
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:14,197
Well, if we're not enemies, ballerina guy,
then why the heck did you steal our ship?

227
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:17,520
Oh, how dumb are you? Watch it! Listen!

228
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:20,737
If I hadn't taken your little
ship from where it was moored,

229
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,397
what do you think would
have happened to it?

230
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,497
The Marines probably would have seized it.

231
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:27,168
Change that probably
to indefinitely, honey.

232
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:29,997
The Marines have been looking all
over for you guys and your ship.

233
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,477
Every port in the
country's been blockaded!

234
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:33,390
Loguetown!

235
00:10:33,473 --> 00:10:34,303
Hey, hold on.

236
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:37,597
Are you telling us you took the
Going Mary so the Marines wouldn't?

237
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,800
Really? How come?

238
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:42,025
Cause you guys are my friends!

239
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,540
Oh, give me a break, guys!

240
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:47,117
We may have had to fight
on opposite sides of a war,

241
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:49,237
but our friendship will
last all of your turns!

242
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,379
Need help loading?

243
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:53,460
Nope, this is the last
one. Friends? Yeah, right.

244
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,117
Tell the truth, Twinkle Toes.

245
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,737
You and your crew don't have a chance
of getting through that blockade.

246
00:10:57,820 --> 00:11:00,017
But you might, if you had us as allies.

247
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,180
Yeah! Like me!

248
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:02,897
That's right, you got me.

249
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:04,477
But in trying times such as these,

250
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:07,097
we have to band together
under the flag of friendship.

251
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:10,460
If you believe in true
friendship, say aye! Aye!

252
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:15,990
Aye!

253
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:17,840
Straw Hats!

254
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,238
Where are you guys?

255
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:22,520
Miss Hina, we've spotted
the Straw Hat ship.

256
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:25,357
It's near the upper reaches
of the Sandora River.

257
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:27,793
What do you think we should do, Captain?

258
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,440
Attack, of course.

259
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:33,680
Igaram, I will!

260
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:39,160
I will be Queen of the Pirates! SCREAM!

261
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,010
Baby!

262
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:03,760
Oh, good morning, Igaram.

263
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,937
What's the matter?

264
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,720
You're sweating. Enough!

265
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:07,910
Where are your manners?

266
00:12:07,993 --> 00:12:09,617
You can't just barge in here.

267
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,457
The princess needs her privacy.

268
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:12,370
Now go!

269
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,519
Please forgive me.

270
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:15,960
I just wanted to say good morning.

271
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,160
Is that all?

272
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:18,837
No, I mean, yes.

273
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:19,937
Quit blabbering!

274
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,357
What are you still doing here?

275
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:22,980
I told you to get out!

276
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,700
I guess it was my imagination.

277
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:28,670
Huh?

278
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,700
Oh, your majesty.

279
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,433
I didn't see you there.

280
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:33,450
Good morning.

281
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:35,540
Yes, good morning.

282
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,240
You too, huh?

283
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,485
Terracotta can be quite scary.

284
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,581
What did you do?

285
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:41,740
Try to say hello?

286
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:44,860
I don't know.

287
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:47,140
Terracotta, isn't this too tight?

288
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:50,848
This is how formal attire is
supposed to fit upon a princess.

289
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:54,597
I heard that the square
is already full of people.

290
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:55,510
Really?

291
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:58,677
When it was announced that your
speech would begin promptly at ten,

292
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:00,701
everyone started getting anxious.

293
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,687
No one wants to miss a word.

294
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:04,477
Your coming-of-age ceremony should have

295
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:06,877
been held two years ago
when you were fourteen.

296
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,397
Since it was delayed so long,

297
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:11,817
it's made the people even more
excited for this special event.

298
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,857
But I don't have any pressing
information to share with them.

299
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:17,116
They're coming because they love you.

300
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,184
You don't have to say one word.

301
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:22,757
All you do is show up and let
everyone see how much you've grown.

302
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:26,537
The Coming of Age ceremony is held
to celebrate you becoming an adult.

303
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:27,977
It's not about speeches,

304
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:32,117
and you should be mindful of the king's
feelings in taking the time for it.

305
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,030
Oh, yeah.

306
00:13:33,113 --> 00:13:35,597
I heard your speech today is
going to be broadcast throughout

307
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:38,717
all of Alabasta with transponder
snails and amplifiers.

308
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,630
How exciting!

309
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,400
I'm really looking forward to it.

310
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:46,700
I received a report that a battle
broke out at the harbor. I see.

311
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:50,569
In light of this, you realize
we can no longer get involved.

312
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,320
Fire! Fire!

313
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:57,180
Damn it!

314
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:58,380
Shoot cannonballs!

315
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:00,305
I can't deflect pointy things!

316
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,748
Seriously, give me a break!

317
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:06,397
If we take any more iron spears
to the bottom of the ship,

318
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:09,186
it'll just be a matter
of time before we sink.

319
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:10,710
More!

320
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:18,077
Hey, I can't keep putting
these holes, you guys!

321
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,117
Don't just stand there and do something!

322
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,376
What more can we do?

323
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:24,048
It takes all our effort
to protect one side!

324
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:27,620
One ship versus eight isn't a fair fight!

325
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:31,551
If this was hand-to-hand combat,
we'd have a better chance.

326
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,470
We're stuck.

327
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:36,899
Whether we chase them or run away,
they won't change their formation.

328
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:43,780
The Black Spear Formation.

329
00:14:43,980 --> 00:14:45,200
It's a work of art.

330
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:48,879
It's the Black Cage Unit Specially!

331
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:50,650
Idiots!

332
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:51,860
Hey, hypnotist!

333
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:54,360
I thought you were a pirate! I am!

334
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:56,017
Now why don't you shut up?

335
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,394
My reasons are my own.

336
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:59,385
Where do I know that guy from?

337
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:01,857
It took a long time,
but I finally found him.

338
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:05,528
That annoying, crazy cook and
his gang of violent cutthroats.

339
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:09,220
Here, today, I vow to sink him.

340
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,160
Stare at this ream.

341
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:14,757
You're about to help me finally
prove that I'm not a weirdo.

342
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:18,134
In fact, my services alone
will pave the way to victory.

343
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:21,940
One, two.

344
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:27,630
Oh!

345
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:29,010
Brother!

346
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:33,590
Whoa!

347
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,120
Usopp, did you do that?

348
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:37,570
Amazing!

349
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,257
Yes, just as I calculated.

350
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:41,170
It was me!

351
00:15:41,253 --> 00:15:42,937
That's what happens to enemy
ships when I'm on the job!

352
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:43,850
Yeah!

353
00:15:43,933 --> 00:15:44,763
That was amazing, Nosy!

354
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,637
The ships in the south have all sunk.

355
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:49,602
Now nothing can prevent
us from breaking through!

356
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:50,990
Oh!

357
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:52,210
Buncle!

358
00:15:52,293 --> 00:15:53,720
We got trouble. What's wrong?

359
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,360
Black Cage!

360
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:57,900
What's going on?

361
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:59,100
Black Cage, Hina!

362
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:00,257
She's a marine captain.

363
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,869
We're in her jurisdiction.

364
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,920
She's a real pain.

365
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,017
We need to hurry up and fly the coop.

366
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,840
Yes, sir, Mr. Bon Clay, sir.

367
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:10,977
Seems we've weakened them quite a bit.

368
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:14,137
There's no ship we can't take down
using our Black Cage formation.

369
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:15,632
Don't get too confident.

370
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:19,477
Underestimating criminals such as these
can come at the expense of one's own life.

371
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,977
now remember once we
arrive you guys are to

372
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:24,137
stay back or you might
get in my way and then

373
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,957
Hina would be annoyed yes ma 'am you guys

374
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:30,177
need to wake up we have
to run if we can pass

375
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:32,097
through that point in
the south we can escape

376
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:34,457
but if we don't change course immediately

377
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:37,177
they'll take us down for
sure if you want to go

378
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:41,797
go we can't go that way
and exactly why not Mr.

379
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:45,737
Bon Clay we Need to set sail while we still
can there's no more time sir noon at the

380
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:48,297
Eastern Harbor we've got An appointment

381
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,337
there's no time to go
around we'll go straight

382
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:55,137
through what Suicide
it's ludicrous is there

383
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:56,717
some treasure you're not
telling me about This

384
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,277
we're throwing away
your lives fine run off

385
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:01,948
and die we have to go
get one Of our friends

386
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:14,940
So, it's for your pal
that you risk it all.

387
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:26,189
Vivi, I'm coming in, okay?

388
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:27,754
Sure, the door's open.

389
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:30,719
Sweetie, what did you want to talk?

390
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,020
Phoebe, amazing.

391
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,697
I mistook you for the queen and her youth.

392
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:40,197
Uncanny resemblance and just as beautiful.

393
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:42,000
A vision of elegance.

394
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:43,438
Have a seat, Daddy.

395
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,010
No.

396
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,060
Father, Igaron. Hmm?

397
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,800
I have an important matter to discuss.

398
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,740
Great Bon Clay!

399
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:01,460
Running now would go against
everything Bon Clay stands for.

400
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:05,779
If we abandon allies who are risking
their lives to pick up a friend,

401
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,195
could we live with ourselves tomorrow?

402
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:12,980
Listen, guys.

403
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,580
Straw Hats, too.

404
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,820
What I must say is of great importance.

405
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:25,840
Miss Hina, the enemy
ships are splitting up.

406
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:27,517
The duck ship is headed south.

407
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:29,835
The duck is probably meant as a decoy.

408
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:30,830
Well,

409
00:18:30,913 --> 00:18:34,897
actually, it appears the entire Strawhead
crew is on board the duck ship, Captain.

410
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:37,745
It's the sheep ship
they're using as the decoy.

411
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:41,600
Follow the duck.

412
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:43,822
Return to formation immediately.

413
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:53,160
Three minutes.

414
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:57,960
Prepare to attack. Ready?

415
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,400
Full speed ahead!

416
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:02,100
So tell me something.

417
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:05,458
I am the Straw Hat you idiots
are looking for, right?

418
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:07,860
Oh, Emma!

419
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:11,560
Miss Hina, the sheep ship
is heading east. What?

420
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:20,257
You must be feeling pretty stupid right
now falling for such a simple trick.

421
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:22,560
See, we're masters of disguise.

422
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:27,800
as well as friends to the Straw Hat.

423
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:36,980
Even if I stray from my code as a man?

424
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:40,840
Even if I stray from my code as a woman?

425
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:44,400
I could never betray my basic humanity.

426
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:48,340
That is the difference between us.

427
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:52,320
If my brethren and I are to
fall, we will fall together?

428
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:56,060
clinging to our freedom
and watching its bloom.

429
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,440
By Bunkley.

430
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:12,900
Bring it on, sister.

431
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,620
Hina's humiliated.

432
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:23,000
Whoop!

433
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:46,260
Buckley!

434
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:49,770
Huh?

435
00:20:57,220 --> 00:21:03,280
I promise you, Vaughn Blaine,
we will never forget you!

436
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:15,937
If we are to fall, let it be in the sea.

437
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:19,557
The flower of friendship is rejoicing.

438
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:22,897
We don't know who the ringleader is.

439
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:23,917
Right?

440
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,917
It's an underground organization.

441
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:30,177
Even its members know absolutely nothing
about the identity of their boss.

442
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:32,877
So this country's enemy has no name.

443
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:36,377
It's impossible for us to gather
information on them from the outside.

444
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:39,637
Further investigation might
put the country at risk.

445
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:40,937
But we do have a lead.

446
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:42,540
Isn't that correct? Yes.

447
00:21:45,260 --> 00:21:47,857
Igaram, do you know what
I'm thinking right now?

448
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:50,240
No, no, I don't! Leave me be!

449
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:54,280
I have to go back to my
work! Igaram! No! Stop it!

450
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,537
This isn't a game!

451
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:58,032
All the more reason to be honest with me!

452
00:21:58,620 --> 00:22:00,620
I can't sit around and do nothing!

453
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,470
Ah!

454
00:22:16,553 --> 00:22:17,853
They're after us again!

455
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:20,560
Get out of our way!

456
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:23,690
Look!

457
00:22:23,773 --> 00:22:24,700
There she is!

458
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:26,180
It's Vivi!

459
00:22:26,280 --> 00:22:27,877
Princess Vivi, you're a vision!

460
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:28,840
We love you!

461
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:32,670
Princess!

462
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:34,980
She's all grown up! Princess!

463
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:47,800
Then, Vivi, let me ask
you just one question.

464
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,880
It all started on that day.

465
00:22:52,260 --> 00:22:54,920
Are you prepared to live at all cost?

466
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:59,820
I went on a little adventure.

467
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:03,217
Princess Vivi's speech has started.

468
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:04,130
Hurry up!

469
00:23:04,213 --> 00:23:05,577
I've been waiting so long!

470
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:07,180
Oh, it's so exciting!

471
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:10,517
The ceremony in Alabana
has finally started.

472
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,337
That was delayed by two hours.

473
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:13,250
What happened?

474
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:17,070
Ah, well.

475
00:23:17,153 --> 00:23:19,629
I can only hope it
won't cause a commotion.

476
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:21,160
Come and listen, Koza!

477
00:23:21,420 --> 00:23:22,400
Hey, come on!

478
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:24,457
Phoebe's speech has already started!

479
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:26,437
The amplifiers are cranked all the way up.

480
00:23:26,520 --> 00:23:29,402
I could be underground
and still hear every word.

481
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:34,900
A journey to cross the Dark Sea, but
what I found was a grand adventure.

482
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:38,137
The sheer vastness of the
ocean was overwhelming,

483
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:41,808
and yet it brought me to a series
of islands so unbelievable.

484
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,480
They defied imagination.

485
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:48,540
With such wondrous environments,
inhabited by strange creatures.

486
00:23:48,980 --> 00:23:54,100
At times, the melody of the waves was
quiet, swaying gently as if easing my soul.

487
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:59,220
And there were other times, when the
melody was violently laughing at me,

488
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:02,126
as if threatening to rip
my very heart in two.

489
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:09,820
In that dark, dark storm, I
encountered a single, small ship.

490
00:24:10,540 --> 00:24:13,860
The ship spoke to me
while pushing me onward.

491
00:24:14,140 --> 00:24:18,460
It said with a clear, singular
voice, Can't you see the light?

492
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:20,700
This wondrous ship,

493
00:24:20,860 --> 00:24:24,684
which never strayed off course
even through pitch-black darkness,

494
00:24:25,060 --> 00:24:27,600
danced its way across the huge waves.

495
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:31,297
The mighty ship kept its
stem pointed straight ahead,

496
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:34,960
thwarting every obstacle
the ocean could throw at.

497
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:41,060
Finally, as the ship roused my spirits,
it said, Look, there is a light.

498
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:45,767
History will one day catalogue
this experience as an illusion,

499
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:49,680
but I will always remember
it as a singular truth.

500
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:51,531
What's she talking about?

501
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:55,488
The secret battle she fought
against that group of criminals.

502
00:24:56,300 --> 00:24:57,130
And...

503
00:25:00,580 --> 00:25:01,410
Vivi!

504
00:25:01,740 --> 00:25:02,817
Forget about it.

505
00:25:02,900 --> 00:25:03,997
You heard the speech.

506
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:06,117
That was Vivi's voice without a doubt.

507
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,877
They're just broadcasting the ceremony
that's being held in Alubarna.

508
00:25:09,960 --> 00:25:12,537
Vivi's already made up
her mind not to come here.

509
00:25:12,620 --> 00:25:14,277
No, I don't buy it.

510
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:15,360
I say she's here.

511
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:18,360
This is the Tamarisk place, right?

512
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:22,420
Yeah, that's it. Let's go. It's past noon.

513
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:24,257
There's no way she wouldn't have come.

514
00:25:24,340 --> 00:25:25,417
She's definitely here.

515
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,077
Let's get out and look for her.

516
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:27,990
This is bad, guys.

517
00:25:28,073 --> 00:25:29,864
The Marines are after us again.

518
00:25:29,980 --> 00:25:31,977
Exactly how many ships are out there?

519
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:33,320
I see at least six.

520
00:25:33,580 --> 00:25:34,756
Damn it, let's move.

521
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:36,799
Give it up, Luffy.

522
00:25:37,440 --> 00:25:40,440
Vivi's course is on a road
far different from ours.

523
00:25:44,580 --> 00:25:46,580
Let me know what's going on, Vivi.

524
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:49,380
What the hell is going on?

525
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:51,640
Hey, show your face!

526
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:53,114
We know you're a fake!

527
00:25:53,420 --> 00:25:55,340
It's Squad Captain Igaram!

528
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:56,880
Where's the real Vivi?

529
00:25:57,260 --> 00:26:01,260
We heard her voice, so where the
hell is the princess sneaking from?

530
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:07,180
At least Vivi is safe.

531
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:09,930
Everyone!

532
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:23,830
Vivi!

533
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:25,390
Karoo!

534
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:28,790
Vivi!

535
00:26:28,873 --> 00:26:30,660
See, she came! Silver!

536
00:26:31,420 --> 00:26:32,297
We need to go back!

537
00:26:32,380 --> 00:26:33,210
Better hurry!

538
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:35,656
The Marines are right behind us, too!

539
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:42,380
I came to say goodbye!

540
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:46,720
What'd she say?

541
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:48,080
Karoo, handset.

542
00:26:51,180 --> 00:26:53,777
Sorry but I can't go with you.

543
00:26:53,860 --> 00:26:56,100
Thank you so much for everything!

544
00:26:57,820 --> 00:26:59,597
Who's the princess talking to?

545
00:26:59,680 --> 00:27:00,637
No way.

546
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:02,657
I think I just spotted princess Vivi.

547
00:27:02,740 --> 00:27:05,417
She's supposed to be at
the ceremony in Alubarna.

548
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:07,817
I'd like to go on more adventures.

549
00:27:07,900 --> 00:27:12,997
But I can't ignore the needs of my
country which I love more than anything.

550
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:14,537
Where is Vivi?

551
00:27:14,620 --> 00:27:18,700
We want our princess, not a
captain in disguise! Hey, princess!

552
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:19,980
You need a shade!

553
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,160
Ma-ma-ma!

554
00:27:21,580 --> 00:27:23,320
Nice dancing, he girl!

555
00:27:24,380 --> 00:27:25,457
Yeah, keep it up!

556
00:27:25,540 --> 00:27:27,658
Everyone can tell those aren't real!

557
00:27:29,340 --> 00:27:30,677
I have to stay.

558
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:32,054
I hope you understand.

559
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:34,050
I see.

560
00:27:34,620 --> 00:27:35,460
Thank you.

561
00:27:37,220 --> 00:27:41,017
Our sign needs to be an X.
How come? We're pirates!

562
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:45,177
You know that it's literal translation
means death to one's opponents, right?

563
00:27:45,260 --> 00:27:46,090
That's fine.

564
00:27:46,173 --> 00:27:47,220
It must be an X.

565
00:27:47,340 --> 00:27:48,920
It looks cool. Covey.

566
00:27:49,140 --> 00:27:50,340
Yeah, I like it.

567
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:52,297
It doesn't matter what it is.

568
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:53,417
That's not the point.

569
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:54,330
Just write it.

570
00:27:57,960 --> 00:27:58,800
I will.

571
00:28:05,160 --> 00:28:05,990
I...

572
00:28:06,073 --> 00:28:06,903
this will do.

573
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,880
I will remain here and fulfill my duty.

574
00:28:12,500 --> 00:28:14,300
It's a sign of our friendship.

575
00:28:15,820 --> 00:28:17,520
If we ever meet again?

576
00:28:18,940 --> 00:28:20,957
No matter how much time's passed!

577
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:22,805
will you still call me friend?

578
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,120
Did you hear that?

579
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:34,097
The princess has some kind
of bond with the Straw Hacks.

580
00:28:34,180 --> 00:28:35,010
Yeah.

581
00:28:35,093 --> 00:28:36,917
Princess Vivi considers
those pirates friends?

582
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,080
You forever idiot!

583
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:40,780
Don't reply, got it?

584
00:28:41,100 --> 00:28:43,460
The Marines now know about Vivi and us.

585
00:28:43,900 --> 00:28:47,277
If they can prove she has a
connection to us, it's all over.

586
00:28:47,360 --> 00:28:49,242
She'll be considered a criminal.

587
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:52,100
Turn away, not another word.

588
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:35,424
No matter what happens
on that island, remember,

589
00:29:35,580 --> 00:29:39,320
this thing on all our arms
is a sign of our friendship.

590
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:11,017
Ah!

591
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:16,080
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

592
00:30:16,860 --> 00:30:21,120
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

593
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:23,720
One piece.
